---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookies"
  description="alexemm.com sets no cookies and uses no tracking. Here is what that means and what would change it."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-09')}
>

  <h2>This site does not use cookies</h2>

  <p>
    Not analytics cookies, not preference cookies, not "strictly necessary" cookies.
    None.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is why there is no consent banner. Under the ePrivacy rules, implemented in
    Cyprus by Section 99(5) of Law 112(I)/2004, consent is required before a site
    stores information on your device or reads information already stored there. This
    site does neither, so there is nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <h2>What that also means</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>No tracking pixels, no fingerprinting, no session recording.</li>
    <li>
      No third-party scripts of any kind. Fonts are served from this domain, not from
      Google.
    </li>
    <li>
      No embedded content that could set cookies on someone else's behalf. No YouTube
      players, no maps, no social feeds, no comment widgets.
    </li>
    <li>No advertising, and nothing on this site has been paid for by anyone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Local storage</h2>

  <p>
    The site may use your browser's local storage for one thing only: remembering
    whether you chose light or dark mode, so you do not have to choose again. That
    preference never leaves your device, is not personal data, and is exempt from
    consent because it is a preference you actively set.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you clear your browser data it disappears, and the site falls back to whatever
    your operating system prefers.
  </p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>

  <p>
    If I ever add analytics, it will be a cookieless, privacy-respecting one, and this
    page will say so before it goes live. If I ever add something that genuinely
    requires consent, you will get a proper consent mechanism, not a banner that
    assumes your agreement.
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
